' 12. Edit and publish a lesson (admin)
' Use case: Manage lessons → Edit draft, Preview, Publish, Restore original (Manage content) · Actor: Admin
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Unit of work: publishing (published version + draft removed + audit log entry) is one transaction
'     (services/lesson-edit.service.ts)
'   - Chain of responsibility: authenticate → requireAdmin on every admin route
'   - Repository
'   Design choice worth a note: the learner's web app keeps the last published copy, so lessons still show the
'   edits when the server can't be reached.
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 12 Edit and publish a lesson
title 12. Edit and publish a lesson (admin)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Admin
boundary "Admin web app" as AdminWeb
control "Moderation\ncontroller" as Ctrl
control "Lesson-edit\nservice" as Svc
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
boundary "Learner's web app" as LearnerWeb
actor Learner

note over AdminWeb, Ctrl : «Chain of responsibility»: authenticate → requireAdmin → controller

Admin -> AdminWeb : Content → Lesson editor → a lesson
AdminWeb -> Ctrl : GET /api/admin/lessons/:lessonId/edit
Ctrl -> Svc : course version + draft + published edit
Svc -> Repo : SELECT lesson_edits
Ctrl --> AdminWeb : lesson to edit

Admin -> AdminWeb : edit text, vocabulary, conversation, questions
AdminWeb -> Ctrl : PUT /api/admin/lessons/:lessonId/draft
Ctrl -> Svc : saveDraft() → validate
alt problems found
  Svc --> AdminWeb : 400 + every problem listed
end
Svc -> Repo : save draft
Admin -> AdminWeb : Preview, then Publish
AdminWeb -> Ctrl : POST /api/admin/lessons/:lessonId/publish
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Svc -> Repo : draft becomes the published version
  Svc -> Repo : audit log entry
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE / INSERT …
end
Ctrl --> AdminWeb : published

Learner -> LearnerWeb : open the site
LearnerWeb -> Ctrl : GET /api/site/lesson-edits
Ctrl --> LearnerWeb : published edits
LearnerWeb -> LearnerWeb : apply edits to every lesson page, keep a copy for offline
LearnerWeb --> Learner : lesson shows the new text

opt Restore original
  Admin -> AdminWeb : Restore original
  AdminWeb -> Ctrl : DELETE /api/admin/lessons/:lessonId/published
  Svc -> Repo : remove published edit + audit log entry
end
@enduml
